From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Flysoft <flysoftbeta@outlook.com>
Date: Wed, 21 Oct 2026 12:43:31 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 33/34] WIP: retain PRTS pipe cancellation through thread-pool
 shutdown

Stop currently posts cancellation and worker joins as CONTINUE_ON_SHUTDOWN, so process exit may discard the task while synchronous pipe reads remain pending. Use BLOCK_SHUTDOWN for this cleanup. Native strict shutdown qualification is pending build47; no exit gate is changed.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>

diff --git a/chrome/browser/prts/prts_pipe_client_win.cc b/chrome/browser/prts/prts_pipe_client_win.cc
index 415fc30540..ce7490347a 100644
--- a/chrome/browser/prts/prts_pipe_client_win.cc
+++ b/chrome/browser/prts/prts_pipe_client_win.cc
@@ -309,7 +309,9 @@ void PrtsPipeClient::Stop() {
   base::ThreadPool::PostTask(
       FROM_HERE,
       {base::MayBlock(), base::WithBaseSyncPrimitives(),
-       base::TaskShutdownBehavior::CONTINUE_ON_SHUTDOWN},
+         // Finish cancelling inherited synchronous pipe I/O before process
+         // shutdown can discard this task and leave the reader in ReadFile.
+         base::TaskShutdownBehavior::BLOCK_SHUTDOWN},
       base::BindOnce(
           [](std::shared_ptr<State> state) {
             for (base::Thread* thread : {&state->reader, &state->writer}) {
